Description: VeltOS Graphics Cards: graphics card drivers in one window
 Finds the PC's NVIDIA, AMD and Intel graphics cards and shows each with
 the driver it uses and its properties (model, board, PCI ID, kernel
 driver and version, video memory, OpenGL renderer, Mesa and Vulkan).
 .
 One button installs or updates what the card needs, from Debian's
 archive through PackageKit (the administrator's password goes through
 polkit): NVIDIA's proprietary driver (the series nvidia-detect
 recommends, built by DKMS, with Secure Boot key registration through
 mokutil) or the AMD/Intel firmware and Mesa's OpenGL and Vulkan drivers.
 Virtual machines' displays need nothing and say so.
